Article 13 (1) The Regent establishes the Management of the Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A).

2. The establishment of Management as referred to in paragraph (1) is stipulated by Regent's Decree including the secretariat container for management and the provision of supporting facilities for the implementation of activities.

Article 14 (1) The Management of the Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment (P2TP2A) consists of leadership elements and members stipulated by Regent's Decree.

2. Leadership elements include: a. chairperson;
b. secretary; and c. treasurer.
3. Membership elements are divided into the form of: a. service field b. information field;
c. accompaniment field;
d. education and training field.

Article 15 (1) The Center for Protection and Empowerment of Women and Children in carrying out its functions builds a working network with: a. Police; b. Prosecutor's Office;
c. Court;
d. Witness and Victim Protection Agency; e. Hospital/Community Health Center;
f. Other institutions that have the same objectives.
2. In addition to building a working network as referred to in paragraph (1), cooperation can be carried out with: a. Government;
b. Provincial Government;
c. Other Regency/City Governments; and d. Non-Governmental Institutions. e. International institutions whose existence is recognized.
3. Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2), is set forth in the form of a joint agreement.

Article 16 (1) The Center for Protection and Empowerment of Women and Children establishes partnerships with the business world for support in organizing protection for women and children in the Regional area.

2. Partnerships as referred to in paragraph (1), are in the form of: a. information and opening of employment opportunities; b. provision of education and job training; c. provision of educational assistance for women and children victims of acts of violence; and

d. provision of independent business capital assistance.

Article 17 The Regent as the person responsible for the protection and empowerment of regional women and children has the authority to make changes to the management or dismissal of members if the existing management or members do not carry out their roles and functions.

CHAPTER VIII PUBLIC PARTICIPATION

Article 18 (1) The public may participate in providing protection and empowerment to women and children victims of violence, neglect and trafficking in persons.

2. Public participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of: a. providing information to authorized officials or institutions;
b. assisting in the rescue of women and children;
c. providing basic and or specific needs assistance for women and children;
d. forming family partners or small units at the village/sub-district level that actively work together to protect the environment of women and children from acts of violence;
e. independently socializing the rights of women and children;
f. providing legal assistance and advocacy.
3. Public participation in providing protection and empowerment of women and children shall be carried out responsibly in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

