3. Improving economic enterprises as referred to in paragraph (1) by providing:

a. work skills training;

b. productive economic enterprise training and joint business groups;
c. accompaniment in the development of productive economic enterprises;

d. capital assistance; and e. ease of access to information and marketing promotion of productive economic production results.

Article 9 Child victims of violence whose parental custody rights have been revoked, their education becomes the responsibility of the Regional Government or foster parents who obtain custody rights from a court decision.

CHAPTER IX GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION

Article 19 (1) The Regent shall conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of regional protection and empowerment of women and children.

2. The public is authorized to actively supervise the implementation of regional protection and empowerment of women and children.
3. The authority of the public as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be in the form of: a. providing input; b. asking questions and obtaining answers from responsible regional government officials;
c. requesting realization and concrete activities from those assigned tasks and authority;
d. other matters that are constructive and provide solutions.

